<title>GERMANY: Buba says west German Q1 GDP rises 0.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Buba says west German Q1 GDP rises 0.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank gave the following details of Q4 1996 GDP data:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP   Q1 97    Q4 96    Q3 96</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    +0.4     +0.1     +0.7</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+2.8     +2.2     +1.8</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)     775.6    772.2    771.6</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    +0.7     +0.1     +0.7</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+2.6     +2.1     +1.7</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)     704.3   699.4    698.9</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    -1.9     +0.1     +1.0</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+4.4     +3.0     +3.1</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)     71.3     72.7     72.6</p>
<p>NOTE - The changes in the table are calculated by Reuters from the Bundesbank GDP data. The figures are seasonally adjusted. The Federal Statistics Office and the Bundesbank earlier gave the qtr/qtr figures rounded to the nearest half pct point.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
